            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "brimstone06"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Brilliant recipe! It was a definite hit and very more-ish. \n\nI made a couple of changes simply because of what was on hand - I grated Red Leicester cheese from the block and used light cream cheese. I also ended up only making half a recipe but it scaled down beautifully. \n\nI would recommend trying to grate the red pepper and onion - even though it turns the ingredients into a sort of mush, they then blends into the cheese smoothly and evenly."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karensg1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been making this cheese ball for years and the secret is to put some cayenne pepper in it (depending on how hot you want it). I usually put in a teaspoon. Every time I make it, someone asks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2017-12-15T18:03:42.400Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda Merrill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It takes Tablespoons (not teaspoons) of the lemon juice and Worcestershire sauce to give it any zing at all. I used green and red bell pepper to give it a holiday flair. Cover it all in pecan pieces. Can't be beat!",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-14T22:02:54.343Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
